speechtext:
I have a few more questions. It may also be that in Ontario we are going to make use of other systems of teaching. It might be wise if we gave consideration to the matter of teaching by television. It may be that the federal government will pioneer in this field and be of a great deal of assistance, particularly in those areas where the national government has a responsibility with regard to education, the vocational training field. It may be that the national government should decide now on the standards of training and the type of training that should be given in each of these vocational schools. Perhaps the government should set standards in order to give guidance to those provinces that have not had as much experience in this type of training as other provinces.
Before the program can really be called a vocational and technical training program I think there must also be established a set of qualifications for teachers on a national basis;

because 1 am sure, as other Ontario members are, that in the vocational schools this year there are going to be many teachers with a very limited amount of training in the particular fields concerned. As I pointed out yesterday, this is a fact now in many of the small high schools that have vocational training programs. The people they are getting are receiving quite high salaries although they have very limited qualifications for training other people in these fields. This is true of most of the areas of which I am aware.
